# Nucleus Sync: Product Specifications
**Vision:** Frictionless context synchronization across all agentic surfaces.

## The 5-Tier Sync Model

| Tier | Scope | Requirement | Implementation Strategy | Status |
|:---|:---|:---|:---|:---|
| **1** | **Across Chats** (Same Machine) | **Must Have** | **Filesystem SSOT** (Single Source of Truth). All chats read/write to `~/.gemini/.../brain`. | ✅ Supported (v0.4.0)* |
| **2** | **Across IDEs** (Same Machine) | **Must Have** | **Filesystem SSOT**. VS Code / Cursor extensions connect to same MCP server/paths. | ✅ Supported (v0.4.0)* |
| **3** | **Across CLI** (Same Machine) | **Must Have** | **Filesystem SSOT**. `nucleus-cli` tool reads same paths. | ✅ Supported (v0.4.0)* |
| **4** | **Via GCloud** (Integration) | *Good to Have* | **CLI Wrapping**. Nucleus wraps `gcloud` to inject cloud state into local context. | 🚧 In Progress (Phase 49) |
| **5** | **Cross-Device** (Different Cloud) | *Pro / Paid* | **Cloud Sync Service**. Replaces local FS with Managed DB (Firestore/Supabase). | 📅 Roadmap (v1.0+) |

*\*Supported via [brain_session_start()](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#3976-4110) protocol. True "Real-Time" without polling requires File Watching (Phase 50).*

## Technical Implementation (Tiers 1-3)
**How it works Natively:**
1.  **Shared State:** The `.brain/` folder IS the database.
2.  **Concurrency:** Atomic file writes (JSON) ensure data integrity.
3.  **Discovery:** Standard path (`~/.gemini/antigravity/brain/{id}`) means zero config for new tools.

**The "Frictionless" Upgrade (Phase 50):**
*   **Current:** Agents must *pull* state ([brain_session_start](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#3976-4110)).
*   **Future:** MCP Server *pushes* updates via **File Watchers** -> **MCP Notifications**.
    *   *Result:* You edit a file in VS Code -> Chat Agent instantly sees "Context Updated".

## Conclusion
Nucleus **natively solves 1-3** today by design (Shared Filesystem).
We are building **4** (Cloud Build / GCloud).
We will sell **5** (Cloud SaaS).
